From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: the process compositor outlives a program's stray release

OneDrive, after "Use this folder", gets Window.Compositor once and releases it twice. On Windows that does no harm, as XAML's own objects (every element's visual) hold the compositor many times; ours held it once, so the compositor ended, and what OneDrive's React Native views made from it afterwards (property sets, expression animations) belonged to an ended compositor whose animations no longer run (6242 kept that from crashing). XAML now takes, when it makes the process compositor, the references its own objects would hold, so a stray release no longer ends it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/composition.c b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/composition.c
index 261125f..017fe9d 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/composition.c
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/composition.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ static const GUID IID_ICompositor_x = { 0xb403ca50, 0x7f8c, 0x4e83, { 0x98, 0x5f
 enum { ICompositor_CreateContainerVisual_x = 9, ICompositor_CreatePropertySet_x = 18 };
 
 static IInspectable *compositor;   /* ICompositor */
+#define XAML_COMPOSITOR_KEEP 64    /* references the framework's own objects would hold */
 static CRITICAL_SECTION compositor_cs;
 static CRITICAL_SECTION_DEBUG compositor_cs_debug =
 {
@@ -70,6 +71,17 @@ HRESULT xaml_compositor( IInspectable **out )
         {
             hr = IInspectable_QueryInterface( inspectable, &IID_ICompositor_x, (void **)&compositor );
             IInspectable_Release( inspectable );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_XAML_COMPOSITOR_ONE_REF
+            /* Windows' XAML keeps its compositor through the many objects of its own made from it
+             * (every element's visual holds it), so a program that releases Window.Compositor once
+             * more than it got it -- OneDrive does, after "Use this folder" -- cannot end it.  Ours
+             * holds it once: the references those objects would hold are taken here instead. */
+            if (compositor)
+            {
+                unsigned int i;
+                for (i = 0; i < XAML_COMPOSITOR_KEEP; i++) IInspectable_AddRef( compositor );
+            }
+#endif
         }
         if (FAILED(hr)) WARN( "no compositor: %#lx\n", hr );
     }
